# Skill: GitHub Action Integration

## When to use

Use this skill when the user wants to:
- add `{{ $cli.Binary }}` to a GitHub Actions workflow
- install a released version or build an unreleased revision of the tool in CI
- dogfood one of the generated subcommand actions from this repository
- run `{{ $cli.Binary }}` commands through an action or after an install-only step

Prefer the actions when one of them already represents the workflow step that needs to be run.
Prefer `actions/{{ $install.DirectoryName }}` when the workflow only needs the tool to be available for later shell commands, loops, or more complex parallel orchestration.
{{ if .OCI.PublishesToGHCR -}}
When workflows prefer containerised execution, reproducible builds, or avoiding local installation entirely, published OCI images from `{{ .OCI.ImageName }}` are also an option.
{{ end }}

